    <h3 style="color: #ffffff; font-size: 1.1rem; font-weight: 700; margin-bottom: 10px; line-height: 1.4;">Diverse Transportation Options:</h3>
    <p style="color: #94a3b8; font-size: 0.88rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0;">Enclosed carriers can be used with different modes of transportation, including trucks, trains, and ships. This flexibility allows you to choose the most suitable mode of transport based on your budget and time constraints.</p>
  </div>
</div>

	<ul>
		<li><strong>Affordability:</strong> Open trailers are typically less expensive than enclosed carriers, making them a popular choice for budget-conscious customers.</li>
		<li><strong>Flexibility:</strong> Open trailers offer greater flexibility in terms of transportation modes, as they can be easily attached to trucks or cars.</li>
		<li><strong>Exposure to Weather Conditions:</strong> The downside of open trailers is that they expose your bike to various weather conditions, such as rain, dust, and wind. This increased exposure increases the chances of scratches, dents, or other damages during transportation.</li>
	</ul>

	<p>In the context of Purnea, enclosed carriers provide the best protection for your two-wheeler vehicle. While open trailers are more affordable and offer greater flexibility, the risk of weather exposure and potential damages outweigh their advantages.</p>

	<p>However, if you are facing budget constraints or have a bike with standard dimensions, open trailers might be a suitable choice. For high-end or customized bikes, we recommend opting for enclosed carriers.</p>

